    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f9fa8fd7_8a3fead3",
        "filename": "cc/cc.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1993,
      "author": {
        "id": 1878380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-06-26T17:26:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I believe so. This relies on the fact that Soong does deduping of apex variants based on min_sdk_version of apexes\n```\ncc_lib{name: somelib}\n\n# apexes containing somelib\ncom.android.foo, min_sdk_version: 29\ncom.android.bar, min_sdk_version: 29\n\ncom.android.baz, min_sdk_version: 30\n```\n\nThis will create two groups of apexInfo\n```\nGroup1: [com.android.foo, com.android.bar], 29\nGroup2: [com.android.baz] 30\n```\n\nI think for the cquery call for `somelib_apex29`, we can pass either of `com.android.foo` _or_ `com.android.bar`. The cflafgs of both these two variants are same (both in Soong and Bazel).\n\nTo test this, I created a mock apex_test module with all the defaults of test_com.android.foo, and this builds fine\n```\napex_test { \n    name: \"com.android.mytest\", \n    manifest: \"test_manifest_codec.json\", \n    file_contexts: \":com.android.media.swcodec-file_contexts\", \n    defaults: [\"com.android.media.swcodec-defaults\"], \n    installable: false, \n}\n```\n\nIs there a specific scenario that you think we should test further?",
      "parentUuid": "d4c5a317_8faf6729",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1992,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 1993,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "da2ae59d76465b9e60e120c785ba5006fa3314c1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
